---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getPacks } from '../../lib/packs';
import { stickerThumb } from '../../lib/thumbs.mjs';

const site = Astro.site?.href ?? 'https://88cutouts.com/';
const packs = await getPacks();

const jsonld = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'CollectionPage',
    name: 'Sticker packs for Instagram Stories',
    url: new URL('/packs/', site).href,
    mainEntity: {
      '@type': 'ItemList',
      numberOfItems: packs.length,
      itemListElement: packs.map((p, i) => ({
        '@type': 'ListItem',
        position: i + 1,
        url: new URL(`/packs/${p.slug}/`, site).href,
        name: p.name,
      })),
    },
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sticker packs for Instagram Stories — copy a whole set at once | 88cutouts"
  description={`${packs.length} themed sticker packs, from beach days and coquette bows to retro music and birthdays. Copy a whole pack into your Story in one tap, free.`}
  image={packs[0]?.entries[0]?.data.image}
  jsonld={jsonld}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span>Sticker packs</p>

    <div class="section-head">
      <h1 class="tool-title">Sticker packs</h1>
      <span class="count">{packs.length} packs</span>
    </div>
    <p class="lede">
      Small themed sets, each picked to dress one Story. Open a pack to copy all of it at
      once as a single sticker, or turn it into a collage with your own words.
    </p>

    <div class="pack-grid">
      {
        packs.map((p) => (
          <a class="pack-card" href={`/packs/${p.slug}/`}>
            <div class="pack-thumbs">
              {p.entries.slice(0, 4).map((s) => (
                <img src={stickerThumb(s.data.image, 200)} alt="" width="200" height="200" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              ))}
            </div>
            <div class="card-meta">
              <div class="card-title">{p.name}</div>
              <div class="card-sub">{p.entries.length} stickers</div>
            </div>
            <p class="pack-blurb">{p.blurb}</p>
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Why packs</h2>
      <p>
        The hard part of decorating a Story isn't finding one nice sticker. It's finding three
        or four that belong together. Stickers picked one at a time tend to clash: a
        photographic flower next to a flat cartoon heart, a pastel bow beside a saturated
        tropical bloom. Each pack here is chosen as a set, with a shared palette and a
        shared way of being drawn or photographed, so anything you take from it goes with
        anything else in it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Copying a pack gives you the whole set arranged as one image. Paste it, scale it
        down and put it in a corner. Or paste it twice, once in each corner, for a framed
        look. If you only want one sticker, every pack page lists them individually as well,
        each with its own copy button and opacity control.
      </p>
      <p>
        Want a pack with words on it? Every pack opens in the
        <a href="/collage-maker/">collage maker</a> limited to that pack's stickers: type a
        name, a date or a two-word caption, and the pack is scattered around it.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
